WEBVTT

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:11.090
Are you eating the customers'
leftovers again, Shindou?

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.720
<i>This really is paradise.</i>

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:24.480
Ah, me. The debt's increased again and
I don't have a hope or dream in the world.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.940
It's good fortune just to be alive, Shindou!

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.030
Don't throw away hope!

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.320
As long as you're alive,
something good will happen one day!

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:33.910
Saiki...

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:36.870
So please be dead tomorrow!

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.620
Shindou!

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.630
You meant to say
"believe in tomorrow," right?

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:52.420
Shindou was crying about something.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.470
Isn't he always, though?

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:58.260
True, it does feel
like Kamakura's bullying of Shindou

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.930
has been getting worse by the day.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.890
It's like that's all Kamakura focuses on.
She hardly does any work.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:08.310
You should tell her like it is
once in a while, Muranushi!

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:10.360
Okay, okay.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.200
Um, don't just bully Shindou
all of the time.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.030
You've got work to do.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.280
Sorry, Muranushi.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:22.790
I don't especially like Yuuta,

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.580
but every time I see
a defenseless creature like that,

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.170
I feel like tormenting them.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:30.750
For some reason or other...

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:36.010
Argue with her, Muranushi!

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:09.980
Jeez, Shiho really is an ogre.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:12.980
I HAVE A FEELING IT'LL GO WELL

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:14.610
Maybe it's better to think an elementary
school student is bullying the boy she likes.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.190
That doesn't cut it!

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:17.940
I can't like the person
who's bullying me!

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.570
Crab miso risotto is up.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.660
Hey, Adachi!
You understand, don't you?

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:27.120
Um... Uh...

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:30.000
I don't really understand.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.210
Adachi?

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:33.170
Hey, Adachi...

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.960
I've been thinking
about this for a while now...

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:36.630
What?

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:40.970
Are you in love with Mura?

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.100
Am I?

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.890
Don't ask me!

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:53.230
Dammit! Don't make me
hit you with a comeback line!

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.900
Look at that!

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.150
Does that make your heart beat fast?

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.900
That?

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.030
Does your chest feel tight?
Are you lovesick? Look!

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:09.750
I do have a pain in my heart.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:11.960
That's a different disease!

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.880
I told you, stop making me
hit you with zingers!

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.880
<i>A comedy duo?</i>

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:19.880
Why do you think Adachi is lovesick?

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:22.050
It seems like he's plain old sick to me.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:23.340
I want to leave early today.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:26.680
After all, when you look
at a specific person

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.640
and various symptoms appear,
that's being lovesick, right?

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:31.980
I feel like that's off somehow.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:36.060
I mean, going by that yardstick,
every time I see Miyakoshi...

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.070
I get a headache.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.320
Higashida just badmouthed me!

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.280
Or at least, that's what I felt!

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.410
I didn't badmouth you.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.660
Yes, you did! I'm positive you did!

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:52.710
Or that's what I felt!

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:54.120
I've thought this for a while now...

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:59.170
but Higashida only acts arrogant
around you, Miyakoshi.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:00.090
Do I?

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:04.300
Well, something changed
after the Valentine's Day incident.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:05.720
Valentine's Day...

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:08.050
The chocolate?! Was it that bad?

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:09.600
It was bad.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.770
Even though you took it home!

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:14.350
True, Higashida was a hero that day.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.270
Only someone who ate that
could understand.

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.480
It was like not fit for human consumption

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.990
or had nothing to do
with humans or... I can't explain it.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:27.120
Or maybe the person
who made it wasn't human.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:28.280
You mean me?

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:33.000
But my mom's a cooking expert,
so maybe I'll be good at it eventually.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.290
That's right, for some reason.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:39.630
I hear she's on TV once in a while,
but what's she like?

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:41.460
I don't know. Adachi...

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:44.090
have you heard of Youko Miyakoshi?

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:48.550
Um... That cooking expert
who doesn't have a shred of sensitivity?

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:50.890
She's your mom?

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:53.770
Mother and daughter are alike
in that regard, huh?

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.310
But is it okay to let Adachi
be assaulted like that?

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.810
If she's totally insensitive,

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:02.070
then Miyakoshi's mom
probably can't do fine chopping.

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:02.980
Yes, she can!

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.820
Does she actually measure out amounts?

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:06.320
Of course! She measures by eye!

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:10.870
My guess is she puts the pot with
the cooked food right on the dining table.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.580
That's enough!

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:15.870
You wouldn't want somebody
trash-talking your parents, would you?

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:17.540
I don't care.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:20.960
My mom can cook!

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:22.090
Well, of course.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:25.670
True, she does a sloppy job
of fine chopping, measures by eye,

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.300
and is bad at arranging food on plates!

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:30.180
We always have to replace knives,
the kitchen is always dirty,

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:31.760
and she quickly resorts to violence—

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:37.390
Huh? Youko Miyakoshi?

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:39.400
What are you doing here, Mom?

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.820
Why are you even working?

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:43.860
Um, welcome.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:46.190
I should have introduced myself first.

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:49.030
I'm Hana's mother, Youko Miyakoshi.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:51.830
YOUKO MIYAKOSHI

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.830
You're the ones
my daughter's been taking care of.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:53.450
N-Nice to meet you.

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:54.740
Hana!

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:58.210
I told you we were going out
to eat with your father on the 18th!

00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.620
That's tomorrow, right?

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.790
Um, today is...

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:04.380
The 17th, right?

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:08.010
You're as lovely as I imagined!

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.590
D-Don't look so happy!

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:10.890
You've got it wrong!

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:14.060
It's not that I'm looking forward to it so much
that I got the date mixed up! Seriously!

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:16.850
From the bottom of my heart,
I couldn't care less about that man!

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:19.890
I swear, he was crying to let us
get together just once this month!

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:22.060
His birthday's on November 31st,

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:24.610
so he pleaded with me
to let him see Hana just this once!

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:25.230
<i>- She's really laying into her husband.
- She's really laying into her husband.</i>

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.280
That man is a pest! I'm telling you!

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:28.780
I swear, I don't care
what happens to him!

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:31.740
Is that right? Pardon me.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:32.990
By the way...

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:37.000
did you know
that November only has 30 days?

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.710
Shut up, you little brat!

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.920
Hana, what's the deal with that brat?
He's pissing me off!

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:42.920
That's Higashida.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:46.340
Higashida. That's the...

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.340
The Higashida who ate my chocolate.

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:53.090
Thank you for always
being so kind to my daughter.

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:54.550
It's polite of you to say so.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.520
Mom, you've never even
eaten a dish I've made!

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.640
I am a cooking pro, after all.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.730
I could tell from just one look.

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:05.690
What you made wasn't edible.
It was beyond human knowledge.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.230
Then I wish you would've stopped her
before she gave it to me.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:09.740
I've got it.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:13.450
Higashida became stronger
after eating that.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.280
It had that benefit?

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.450
In this case, I would call it toxicity.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:20.750
I had it the time before, so maybe
I gained something from it, too?

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.420
What's going on here?

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:24.750
This little brat will probably
never get married

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:26.540
because he finds fault with everything,

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.010
but my daughter's to blame
because she changed his nature?

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:32.430
I'll take responsibility by giving you
my daughter's hand in marriage.

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:36.470
Knock it off! He's a brute! A miscreant!

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:37.180
Don't go to the trouble, Mrs. Miyakoshi.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:38.680
I can't even appreciate the sentiment.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:40.480
Please, think again!

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:44.020
CHOCOLATE

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:45.610
Good morning.

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:47.520
But not early in the morning, Daisuke.

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:50.110
Do you know what time it is?

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:51.240
5 am.

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:52.990
That's right, you sleepyhead.

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:56.530
If I got up any earlier,
I wouldn't have anything to do.

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:57.950
The trouble you give me...

00:08:58.240 --> 00:08:59.410
You see, Miyakoshi?

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:01.450
I sure do!

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.080
I haven't been to your room
in a long time, Higashida.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:07.670
Why did you come here so early?

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:11.720
When I called, your dad said
he works from 4 am.

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:13.840
He doesn't work at all.

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:16.590
The old man gets up early for nothing.

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:18.930
My mom cooked,
so I brought some over.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:22.480
She said to tell you,
"I'm counting on you with Hana!"

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:24.730
So I'm counting on you.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:27.190
<i>I'd like to put a bow on her head
and send her back.</i>

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:30.190
You did what you came here for,
so please go home.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:31.440
Good job.

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:33.400
You know, you really are rude.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:35.280
That's right, Daisuke.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:37.200
She went out of her way to come here.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.160
At least walk with her part of the way.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:40.870
It's still dark outside.

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.330
That's because it's still night.

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:46.080
HOKKAIDO SHRINE

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.460
I like to have peace and quiet
on my day off.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:54.470
Look, Higashida! The morning glow!

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.340
That's morning for you.

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:58.930
Wh-Why are Higashida
and Miyakoshi together now?!

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:02.020
Um... I mean,
it's early in the morning, right?

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:03.390
It can't be by chance!

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:05.230
They're not dating as far as I know,

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:07.600
but they're walking side by side
this early in the morning?

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:10.440
Where in the world are they going
and what are they going to do?

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:11.730
Well, this is far enough.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:12.780
Look, Higashida!

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:14.740
What?

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:16.150
Let's make a wish!

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:17.990
Why?

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:19.160
Because it's a shrine!

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:21.240
But why should we visit it?

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.120
To make a wish, of course!

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.620
Even God won't cure stupidity.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:28.080
That's not it! I wanna pray
to be a good cook!

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:29.000
Then let's go.

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:37.800
Higashida, I forgot my wallet.
Lend me some money.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:38.760
SIGH

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:41.260
- How much?
- Well...

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:42.720
1,000 yen!

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:45.310
1,000 yen... as a monetary offering?

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:46.690
I'm splurging.

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:50.560
It probably isn't going to be enough.

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:58.150
Let's just get this over with
as soon as possible.

00:10:58.150 --> 00:10:59.950
You're the one who complained
about my cooking, remember?

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:03.080
<i>Maybe they are dating...</i>

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:07.750
As least so no one dies from it...

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:10.040
Let me be good at cooking!

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:13.000
No, forget that!

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:17.720
Let Higashida eat my cooking
for the rest of his life!

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:23.100
Why would you wish
for something so evil?

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:27.230
Like you said, 1,000 yen probably
isn't enough to make me a good cook,

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:30.650
so I changed it to capture someone
who'll eat my cooking.

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:34.270
With that wish, you'll probably have
a long life until you die.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:35.570
You should be grateful!

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.110
It's a living hell!

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:40.740
Please take it back! Cancel it right now!

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:43.370
That's against the rules. I can't do that.

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:47.290
Then apologize! Apologize to God!

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.410
A-Apologize?

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:50.420
S-Sorry.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:55.880
Jeez. If "I'm sorry" fixed everything,
we wouldn't need the police.

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:58.420
Just in case,
I'm going to say a prayer, too.

00:11:58.420 --> 00:11:59.090
O-Okay.

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:01.050
<i>That was scary!</i>

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:02.550
All right!

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:07.770
May Miyakoshi become good
at cooking!

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:14.690
Higashida, you're doing that for me...

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:17.980
- It's totally creepy!
- It's for my mind and body.

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:20.320
If it doesn't come true,
please pay me back.

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:26.450
<i>It looks like they're arguing,
so maybe I have the wrong idea...</i>

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:29.290
<i>but going by their wishes alone,
it's pretty obvious...</i>

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:36.460
<i>Let Higashida eat my cooking
for the rest of his life!</i>

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:37.920
<i>Just kidding!</i>

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:43.760
<i>Then I'd better wish for Miyakoshi
to become good at cooking!</i>

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:46.510
<i>- What was that?
- Ow!</i>

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:48.260
<i>- Why, you!
- Ow!</i>

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:50.350
<i>...they're a close-knit couple.</i>

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:54.020
<i>There's no way. In fact, who were they?</i>

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:56.690
Hey!

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:00.070
It's a dog, Mr. Raccoon!

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:01.700
Nagata?

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:04.530
What the heck
are you doing over there?

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:05.490
Hello!

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:07.030
<i>Act natural. Act natural.</i>

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:08.910
T-Taking my dog for a walk.

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:11.500
Wh-What are you two doing?

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.000
Praying for our future...

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:16.540
<i>Don't! If you think about it, you'll lose!</i>

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.000
Oh, I know!

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:21.970
Since you're a guest here,
you should make a wish, too!

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:25.050
Higashida just made
a substantial cash offering,

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:27.350
so I'm sure a lot of the effect
is still left over.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:29.140
B-But...

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:31.810
Go ahead, Nagata.
At this point, anything is okay.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:38.440
U-Um...

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:38.440
She's not a guest.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:40.480
Yes, she is.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:44.610
May you make it a little clearer
as to what kind of relationship that is...

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:52.700
Hey!

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:54.830
You guys are older
and know more than me,

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:56.460
so there's something I wanna ask you.

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:59.840
The happy-go-lucky chief
gets serious for once.

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:00.960
What's up?

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:04.220
If you pray to God at a shrine,
will the wish come true?

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:07.430
I don't especially reject
that kind of thing

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:09.180
when it serves
as emotional support for people.

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:12.140
But I don't believe in ghosts and stuff,

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:16.190
so I don't think praying to God will work
unless you do something to make it work.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:19.900
Wha— Even though I splurged
on the money offering?

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:23.190
It'll come true if you made
a generous money offering, Miyakoshi!

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:25.610
Kamakura! It'll come true
if I made a generous offering?

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:27.700
Money never betrays people.

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:29.700
It doesn't betray people?

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:33.790
Although I think it's more effective
when you use it yourself

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:35.460
or give it to someone else.

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:37.210
Money will never betray you.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:39.960
Then it's pointless
to make a wish to God, huh?

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:43.590
Shiho trusts in money more than God.

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:45.720
R-Really?

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:47.840
Girls, you make it sound
like a really cold world!

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:49.970
Don't destroy this child's dreams!

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:51.970
It'll be okay! Your wish will come true!

00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:53.970
Really? It'll come true?

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:55.770
If wishes didn't come true,

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:58.400
there wouldn't still be temples
and shrines around!

00:14:58.400 --> 00:14:59.770
I'm sure it'll come true!

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.440
Not that I have any grounds to say it...

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:05.400
Thanks to you, Kouno, I feel
like I could make chocolate now!

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:07.900
All right!

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:10.410
Chocolate?

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:13.200
If somebody dies, it's your fault, Kouno.

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:14.490
Don't come crying to Shiho.

00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:19.540
This is for you, Yanagiba.

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:21.630
Chocolate?

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.380
What's up, Naga?

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:27.220
I saw a recipe online that looked good,
so I tried making it myself.

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:28.760
Impressive, Naga.

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:30.800
But you're not gonna give
some to Higashi?

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:33.300
Why?

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.180
You're in love with him, aren't you?

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:39.600
S-So you knew.
I-I kind of feel embarrassed.

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:41.690
Naga...

00:15:41.690 --> 00:15:43.480
Are you the easily readable type?

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:49.030
Cocoa, found in chocolate, is supposedly
effective against fatigue and stress,

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:50.860
so Higashi would probably
be happy to get it.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:52.120
But...

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:55.290
Welcome.

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.410
<i>It's really hard to give it to him.</i>

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:01.250
Higashi, you're gloomy today.

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:02.540
What's wrong?

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:05.130
Miyakoshi made chocolate.

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:06.460
Why?

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:08.670
"If I do it now,
I have a feeling it'll go well."

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:10.430
That's what she said.

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:13.470
Higashi, if you don't want it, give it to me.

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:14.390
Forget it.

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:17.640
Higashi, you hate me.

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:18.890
I do hate you.

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:22.100
I hate you, but I still wouldn't let you
take even a bite of that.

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:23.520
Count yourself lucky.

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:28.610
Naga. Higashi said "I hate you" twice.

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:34.200
Higashida, I heard...

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:35.120
What?

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:38.500
If you don't want to,
you don't have to eat it, right?

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:42.210
Then who the hell is going to eat it?

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:43.960
Are you going to eat it, Kisaki?

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:45.420
No.

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:46.840
Sorry.

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:50.340
Adachi...

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:52.430
Y-Yes?

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:54.390
Here, take this.

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:56.350
What's up?

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:57.470
They're cookies.

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:01.600
Yesterday Miyakoshi said something
about bringing chocolate today...

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:03.560
I'm sorry!

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:05.360
...so I bought these on the way to work.

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:08.110
YORAKU
Black Fire Cookie

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:08.110
- For you too, Kouno.
- Me, too?

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:11.570
After all, I can't just
give it to Adachi, right?

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:15.570
Th-There isn't poison or anything
in here? Just kidding.

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:17.080
There is.

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:19.450
- There is?
- There isn't.

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:22.960
Incidentally, that isn't the same
kind of cookie I gave Adachi.

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:27.090
Adachi has helped me out a lot,
so I put my spirit in there.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:29.550
Dammit! Just you wait!

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:34.130
You wouldn't be wrong if you thought
my true feelings are baked in there.

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:37.220
In fact, maybe it goes
beyond a simple crush.

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:39.310
I can't deny
that you're always on my mind.

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:42.180
Adachi, maybe the fact is that I'm in...

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:43.520
Just kidding.

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:45.230
Well, that became a joke along the way.

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:46.810
From which part?

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:50.030
Here you go, Yuuta!

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:51.940
Wh-What's this for?

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:55.490
Yesterday Miyakoshi said something
about making chocolate,

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:57.410
so Shiho brought you something, too!

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:59.240
Are you happy? You're happy, right?

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:01.120
I-I'm happy.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:02.450
You can open it.

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:03.960
Oh, right.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:08.920
Dog food, 100% beef!

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:13.010
Oh, Yuuta! You're so happy
that you're speechless, right?

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:13.880
Yes, of course!

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.550
It's been about ten years
since you've had beef, right?

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:18.140
Even though your father runs
a butcher's shop!

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:19.220
<i>Huh?</i>

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:23.220
That makes you lower than a dog
that always eats beef, Yuuta.

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:25.270
Even lower than a dog!

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:31.400
I-I guess this is way better than that.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:33.780
I did my very best to make it!

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:36.450
You're just full
of fighting spirit, Hana-hana.

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:38.240
That's because my life is on the line!

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:40.530
What happens if you fail?

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:42.450
Y-Yanagiba!

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:46.670
If I fail... death awaits!

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:49.250
<i>Miyakoshi is really serious about this.</i>

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:50.590
Higashida's death!

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:53.800
Okay, eat it, Higashida!

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:55.340
Eat all of it!

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:59.180
Higashida, do you have any last words?

00:19:00.010 --> 00:19:04.390
No. It feels like if I did say them,
I wouldn't be able to come back.

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:07.020
Here I go.

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:18.110
Time for last words!

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:20.910
Bitter...

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:23.280
and spicy.

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:27.580
Higashida...

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:31.170
Higashida! I used
the sweet curry! Seriously!

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:33.590
<i>Sweet curry? In chocolate?</i>

00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:47.270
<i>Higashida...</i>

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:48.730
<i>Higashida...</i>

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:50.520
<i>Higashida...</i>

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:54.020
<i>Higashida, yay!</i>

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:57.280
- That means nothing!
- Higashida! Higashida!

00:19:57.820 --> 00:19:59.400
<i>This is no good, Higashida.</i>

00:19:59.650 --> 00:20:01.240
<i>You left a monetary offering
at the shrine,</i>

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:04.160
<i>but that's not my religion,
so it's out of my jurisdiction.</i>

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:05.240
<i>Oh, come on.</i>

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:07.200
Typical bureaucrat!

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:12.000
<i>I did want to do something
to help you out,</i>

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:15.170
<i>but after all, I am a priest.</i>

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:17.130
<i>It's not like I'm God,</i>

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:20.970
<i>and it's not even close
to Valentine's Day...</i>

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:22.640
I was careless!

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:29.480
Wh-What's wrong with Higashida?

00:20:29.730 --> 00:20:31.270
Miyakoshi's chocolate...

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:32.520
Chocolate?

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:36.110
BLAZE OF SUFFERING

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:36.110
His last words were "blaze of suffering."

00:20:36.110 --> 00:20:37.980
BITTER AND SPICY

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:37.980
Did he say "bitter and spicy"?

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:39.740
Higashida, are you okay?

00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:42.950
I-I did my best for today, too!

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:45.330
I even got a talisman
to ward off bad luck!

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:46.450
Um, so...

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:48.040
It's God's fault!

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:53.460
<i>If you die here,
it'll ruin the love and peace,</i>

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:56.090
<i>so for now,
I'll return you to the other side.</i>

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:58.840
<i>Be well and do your best, Kousaku.</i>

00:20:57.670 --> 00:20:59.920
KOUSAKU...

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:02.180
DAISUKE

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:02.180
It's Daisuke!

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:06.930
We did it, Higashida! Success!

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:08.640
How do you count that as a success?

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:12.810
Yanagiba... would you accept this?

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:17.190
Naga, isn't that the one
you were gonna give to Higashida?

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:21.070
Yeah, that's why I brought it here,

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:25.320
but I have the feeling that if I gave it
to him now, it would be like harassment.

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:26.410
Naga...

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:27.330
Besides...

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:32.540
I only thought they were dating
because of the cooking thing.

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:33.710
Naga...

00:21:34.120 --> 00:21:36.250
You really are the easily readable type.

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:39.550
Yes, that's the exact amount.

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:42.630
Thank you very much!

00:21:51.390 --> 00:21:52.980
It tastes like chocolate!

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:54.640
That's because it is chocolate.

00:23:25.940 --> 00:23:35.950
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

00:23:26.240 --> 00:23:29.030
And here we finally are, the first preview
with an animal partner.

00:23:29.030 --> 00:23:31.700
<i>Really, nothing beats walking with Hana
in the morning. I hope we can do it again.</i>

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:31.660
Taking care of a pet is hard.

00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:32.990
It's like bearing a big burden
on your shoulders.

00:23:32.990 --> 00:23:34.830
<i>This pressure... You'd better recognize!
How about this? How about this?</i>

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:35.950
Next time, "I'll Try Getting Revenge."

00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:35.950
I'LL TRY GETTING REVENGE
